      "problem": "Solve for $C$ where $\\frac{C-4}{3}=\\frac{C-2}{6}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{C-4}{3} & =\\frac{C-2}{6} \\\\ (C-4)\\cdot 6 & =3\\cdot (C-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we proceed as usual to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(C-4)\\cdot 6 & =3\\cdot (C-2) \\\\ 6C-24 & =3C-6 \\\\ 6C-24-3C & =3C-6-3C \\\\ 3C-24 & =-6 \\\\ 3C-24+24 & =-6+24 \\\\ 3C & =18 \\\\ \\frac{3C}{3} & =\\frac{18}{3} \\\\ C & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $C=6.$",
